Notebook[{Cell["Field-map convention and static-anchor certificate", 
   "Title"], Cell["A self-contained independent certificate for the rotating \
horizontal bridge, raw Q tensor, static field-redefinition direction, and \
signature/curvature conventions", "Subtitle"], Cell["Purpose and scope", 
   "Section"], Cell["This notebook reconstructs four convention-sensitive \
results without importing an MX cache, another notebook, or a proposed target \
potential. It establishes the leading and first-order horizontal NS \
three-form bridge, computes all ten independent components of the corrected \
raw Q tensor from its defining covariant derivative, proves the plus \
alphaPrime/8 direction of both static field redefinitions, and checks the \
mostly-minus heterotic to mostly-plus STU connection and curvature bridge. \
Every executable comment is in English.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Convention ledger", "Section"], Cell["The source fibre and three-form \
conventions are z_STU=-z_old and H_STU=-H_old. Consequently \
h_STU^(0)=-M_het+(Hplus Hminus)^(-1)dOmega wedge Theta. With the final \
+C wedge (d h+F wedge G) Lagrange-multiplier term this is \
h_STU^(0)=-Exp[2 Phi] star5 F3 for the positive Eq. (4.1) potential. Also, \
OmegaPlus_STU=-omegaMinus_heterotic. The curvature changes sign but its \
quadratic invariants do not, so alphaPrime is not sign-flipped. The published \
static profiles are reached by Phi_after=Phi_before+(alphaPrime/8)DeltaPhi \
for both Delta1 and Delta2.", "Text"], Cell["Scalar-map supersession", 
   "Section"], Cell["This notebook fixes the direction and overall factor of \
the two predual torsion-removal redefinitions; it does not certify the later \
postdual final scalar by itself. Notebook 26 supersedes any broader reading. \
It proves that the displayed second postdual scalar map needs an additional \
+(1/8) Exp[-8 varphi/3] Fminus^2 term inside Delta2, changing the Fminus^2 \
coefficient from -3/8 to -1/4 before multiplication by alphaPrime/8. The \
metric, sigma, static torsion-free three-form, and lower-two-form results in \
this notebook are unaffected.", "Text"], Cell["Machine-verifiable calculation", 
   "Section"], Cell[BoxData["(* Self-contained convention and static-anchor \
certificate.\n   This calculation imports no cache, no earlier notebook, and \
no proposed\n   target potential.  Every comparison is reconstructed from the \
displayed\n   leading fields and the stated field-redefinition formulas. \
*)\n\nClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n$HistoryLength = 0;\n$Assumptions = r > 0 && 0 \
< theta < Pi && qplus > 0 &&\n  qminus > 0 && qzero > 0 && Element[a, \
Reals];\n\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- *)\n(* \
1. Leading and first-order horizontal H bridge                         *)\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- \
*)\n\ncoords5 = {t, r, theta, phi, psi};\nn5 = Length[coords5];\nhp = 1 + \
qplus/r^2;\nhm = 1 + qminus/r^2;\nh0 = 1 + qzero/r^2;\nw0 = a/(2 \
r^2);\n\ndOne[v_] := Table[\n  D[v[[j]], coords5[[i]]] - D[v[[i]], \
coords5[[j]]],\n  {i, n5}, {j, n5}];\nwedge11[u_, v_] := Table[u[[i]] v[[j]] \
- u[[j]] v[[i]],\n  {i, n5}, {j, n5}];\nwedge21[q_, v_] := Table[\n  q[[i, \
j]] v[[k]] + q[[j, k]] v[[i]] + q[[k, i]] v[[j]],\n  {i, n5}, {j, n5}, {k, \
n5}];\nSetAttributes[{setAnti2, setAnti3}, HoldFirst];\nsetAnti2[x_, {i_, \
j_}, value_] :=\n  (x[[i, j]] = value; x[[j, i]] = -value;);\nsetAnti3[x_, \
tri_, value_] := Do[\n  x[[Sequence @@ p]] = Signature[p] value, {p, \
Permutations[tri]}];\nzeroTensorQ[x_] := And @@ (TrueQ[FullSimplify[#] == 0] \
& /@ Flatten[x]);\n\nthetaOne[ww_] := {1, 0, 0, ww Cos[theta], \
ww};\ndeltaThetaOne[dww_] := {0, 0, 0, dww Cos[theta], dww};\ntheta0 = \
thetaOne[w0];\nomega0 = {0, 0, 0, w0 Cos[theta], w0};\naSTU0 = \
theta0/hp;\nbOld0 = -theta0/hm;\ngOld0 = FullSimplify[dOne[bOld0]];\ndOmega0 \
= FullSimplify[dOne[omega0]];\nkSquared = 1/(hp hm);\n\n(* The magnetic base \
term is M_het=star4_het dHzero from the source paper. *)\nmMagnetic0 = ConstantArray[0, {n5, \
n5, n5}];\nDo[mMagnetic0[[Sequence @@ p]] =\n   Signature[p] D[h0, r] r^3 \
Sin[theta]/8,\n  {p, Permutations[{3, 4, 5}]}];\n\n(* With z_STU=-z_old and \
H_STU=-H_old, the horizontal field is\n     h_STU^(0)=-M_het-G_old wedge A_STU\n  \
            =-M_het+(Hplus Hminus)^(-1) dOmega wedge Theta\n  \
            =-Exp[2 Phi] star5 F3. \
*)\nrotationIdentityResidual = FullSimplify[\n  wedge21[gOld0, aSTU0] + \
kSquared wedge21[dOmega0, theta0]];\nhCorrect0 = FullSimplify[-mMagnetic0 - \
wedge21[gOld0, aSTU0]];\nhCorrectExpanded0 = FullSimplify[\n  -mMagnetic0 + \
kSquared wedge21[dOmega0, theta0]];\nhObsolete0 = FullSimplify[\n  \
-mMagnetic0 - kSquared wedge21[dOmega0, theta0]];\n\n(* Reconstruct the \
complete six-dimensional three-form in the new fibre\n   basis.  This \
independently checks the horizontal/vertical split. *)\nn6 = 6;\ndzOld = {0, \
0, 0, 0, 0, 1};\na6 = Append[aSTU0, 0];\netaOld = dzOld - a6;\netaSTU = \
-etaOld;\ngOld6 = ConstantArray[0, {n6, n6}];\nDo[gOld6[[i, j]] = gOld0[[i, \
j]], {i, n5}, {j, n5}];\nmMagnetic6 = ConstantArray[0, {n6, n6, \
n6}];\nDo[mMagnetic6[[i, j, k]] = mMagnetic0[[i, j, k]],\n  {i, n5}, {j, n5}, \
{k, n5}];\nhCorrect6 = ConstantArray[0, {n6, n6, n6}];\nDo[hCorrect6[[i, j, \
k]] = hCorrect0[[i, j, k]],\n  {i, n5}, {j, n5}, {k, n5}];\nwedge216[q_, v_] \
:= Table[\n  q[[i, j]] v[[k]] + q[[j, k]] v[[i]] + q[[k, i]] v[[j]],\n  {i, \
n6}, {j, n6}, {k, n6}];\nhOld6 = FullSimplify[mMagnetic6 + wedge216[gOld6, \
dzOld]];\nhSTU6 = FullSimplify[-hOld6];\nhSTUReconstructed6 = FullSimplify[\n \
 hCorrect6 + wedge216[gOld6, etaSTU]];\n\nhorizontalLeadingLedger = <|\n  \
\"HeteroticSourceMagneticComponent\" -> TrueQ[FullSimplify[\n    \
mMagnetic0[[3,4,5]] == -qzero Sin[theta]/4]],\n  \
\"PositiveEq41ThirdPotential\" -> TrueQ[FullSimplify[\n    \
(theta0/h0 /. a -> 0) == {1/h0,0,0,0,0}]],\n  \
\"FinalActionMinusDualityStatic\" -> zeroTensorQ[\n    \
(hCorrect0 /. a -> 0) + mMagnetic0],\n  \
\"LeadingGOldWedgeAIdentity\" -> zeroTensorQ[rotationIdentityResidual],\n  \
\"LeadingHorizontalExpression\" ->\n    zeroTensorQ[hCorrect0 - \
hCorrectExpanded0],\n  \"ObsoleteLeadingRotationSignRejected\" ->\n    \
Not[zeroTensorQ[hCorrect0 - hObsolete0]],\n  \
\"SixDimensionalHorizontalReconstruction\" ->\n    zeroTensorQ[hSTU6 - \
hSTUReconstructed6]\n|>;\n\n(* The exact source formulas in arXiv:2606.31987 \
are now expanded to first\n   order in alphaPrime.  ep is only a formal \
bookkeeping parameter. *)\nzZeroCorrection = qzero^2/(r^2 (r^2 + \
qzero)^2);\nzPlusCorrection = -2 (qplus qminus - 2 a^2/(r^2 + qzero))/\n  \
(r^2 (r^2 + qzero) (r^2 + qminus));\nwCorrection = a qzero/(r^2 (r^2 + \
qzero)^2);\n\nstarDOmega[ww_] := Module[{s = ConstantArray[0, {n5, n5}]},\n  \
setAnti2[s, {2, 5}, 2 ww/r];\n  setAnti2[s, {2, 4}, 2 ww Cos[theta]/r];\n  \
setAnti2[s, {3, 4}, -r D[ww, r] Sin[theta]/2];\n  s];\nkOld[ww_] := \
FullSimplify[\n  -wedge11[Table[D[1/hm, coords5[[i]]], {i, n5}], \
thetaOne[ww]] +\n  starDOmega[ww]/hm];\nmagnetic[zz_] := Module[{m = \
ConstantArray[0, {n5, n5, n5}]},\n  setAnti3[m, {3, 4, 5}, r^3 D[zz, r] \
Sin[theta]/8];\n  m];\n\nwFull = w0 + ep wCorrection;\nzPlusFull = hp + ep \
zPlusCorrection;\nzZeroFull = h0 + ep zZeroCorrection;\naFull = \
thetaOne[wFull]/zPlusFull;\nhDirectFull = -magnetic[zZeroFull] - \
wedge21[kOld[wFull], aFull];\nhDirect1 = FullSimplify[\n  \
Coefficient[Normal@Series[hDirectFull, {ep, 0, 1}], ep]];\na1 = \
FullSimplify[Coefficient[Normal@Series[aFull, {ep, 0, 1}], ep]];\nk1 = \
FullSimplify[\n  Coefficient[Normal@Series[kOld[wFull], {ep, 0, 1}], \
ep]];\nhLedger1 = FullSimplify[\n  -magnetic[zZeroCorrection] - wedge21[k1, \
aSTU0] -\n  wedge21[gOld0, a1]];\na1Expected = FullSimplify[\n  \
(deltaThetaOne[wCorrection] - (zPlusCorrection/hp) \
theta0)/hp];\n\nhorizontalFirstOrderLedger = <|\n  \
\"FirstOrderLeadingVerticalEqualsDOldWinding\" ->\n    zeroTensorQ[kOld[w0] - \
gOld0],\n  \"FirstOrderMomentumVectorExpansion\" -> zeroTensorQ[a1 - \
a1Expected],\n  \"FirstOrderHorizontalSourceLedger\" -> zeroTensorQ[hDirect1 \
- hLedger1]\n|>;\n\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- *)\n(* \
2. All ten independent components of the corrected raw Q tensor       *)\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- \
*)\n\n(* The leading mostly-plus five-dimensional string-frame metric is \
built\n   directly from ds5^2=-Theta^2/(Hplus Hminus)+Hzero dsR4^2. *)\ng5 = \
ConstantArray[0, {n5, n5}];\ng5[[1, 1]] = -1/(hp hm);\ng5[[1, 4]] = g5[[4, \
1]] = -w0 Cos[theta]/(hp hm);\ng5[[1, 5]] = g5[[5, 1]] = -w0/(hp hm);\ng5[[2, \
2]] = h0;\ng5[[3, 3]] = h0 r^2/4;\ng5[[4, 4]] = h0 r^2/4 - w0^2 \
Cos[theta]^2/(hp hm);\ng5[[5, 5]] = h0 r^2/4 - w0^2/(hp hm);\ng5[[4, 5]] = \
g5[[5, 4]] =\n  h0 r^2 Cos[theta]/4 - w0^2 Cos[theta]/(hp hm);\ng5Inverse = \
FullSimplify[Inverse[g5]];\nchristoffel5 = Table[FullSimplify[1/2 Sum[\n    \
g5Inverse[[rho, sig]] (D[g5[[sig, nu]], coords5[[mu]]] +\n      D[g5[[sig, \
mu]], coords5[[nu]]] -\n      D[g5[[mu, nu]], coords5[[sig]]]), {sig, \
n5}]],\n  {rho, n5}, {mu, n5}, {nu, n5}];\n\nfMomentum = \
FullSimplify[dOne[aSTU0]];\nfWinding = FullSimplify[dOne[bOld0]];\nfPlus = \
FullSimplify[\n  Sqrt[hp/hm] fMomentum + Sqrt[hm/hp] fWinding];\nfOneUp[mu_, \
lam_] := Sum[\n  fPlus[[mu, k]] g5Inverse[[k, lam]], {k, \
n5}];\nhTwoOneUp[mu_, nu_, beta_] := Sum[\n  hCorrect0[[mu, nu, k]] \
g5Inverse[[k, beta]], {k, n5}];\nnablaPrime[nu_, rho_, lam_] :=\n  \
D[fPlus[[rho, lam]], coords5[[nu]]] -\n  Sum[christoffel5[[s, nu, rho]] \
fPlus[[s, lam]] +\n    christoffel5[[s, nu, lam]] fPlus[[rho, s]], {s, n5}] \
+\n  1/2 Sum[hTwoOneUp[nu, lam, beta] fPlus[[rho, beta]],\n    {beta, \
n5}];\n\n(* The normalized three-index bracket turns the prefactor 3 into one \
half\n   of the signed six-permutation sum. *)\nqComponent[tri_List] := \
Factor[Cancel[Together[FullSimplify[PowerExpand[\n  1/2 Total[(Signature[#] \
Sum[\n      fOneUp[#[[1]], lam] nablaPrime[#[[2]], #[[3]], lam],\n      {lam, \
n5}]) & /@ Permutations[tri]],\n  Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions]]]]];\n\ntriples10 = Subsets[Range[n5], {3}];\nqValues = \
Association@Table[tri -> qComponent[tri], {tri, triples10}];\nqDenominator = \
(r^2 + qminus)^3 (r^2 + qplus)^3 (r^2 + qzero);\nqExpected[tri_List] := \
Switch[tri,\n  {1, 2, 4}, -2 a (qminus - qplus)^2 r^5 \
Cos[theta]/qDenominator,\n  {1, 2, 5}, -2 a (qminus - qplus)^2 \
r^5/qDenominator,\n  {1, 3, 4}, -a (qminus - qplus)^2 r^6 \
Sin[theta]/qDenominator,\n  {3, 4, 5}, -a^2 (qminus - qplus)^2 r^4 \
Sin[theta]/\n    (2 qDenominator),\n  _, 0];\nqExpectedValues = \
Association@Table[tri -> qExpected[tri],\n  {tri, triples10}];\nqResiduals = \
Association@Table[tri -> FullSimplify[\n    qValues[tri] - \
qExpectedValues[tri]], {tri, triples10}];\nqNonzero = Select[qValues, \
Not[PossibleZeroQ[#]] &];\nqZeroTriples = Select[triples10, \
PossibleZeroQ[qExpected[#]] &];\n\nqLedger = <|\n  \"RawQAllTenEvaluated\" -> \
Length[qValues] == 10,\n  \"RawQExpectedComponents\" -> And @@\n    \
(TrueQ[FullSimplify[#] == 0] & /@ Values[qResiduals]),\n  \
\"RawQOtherSixComponentsZero\" -> And @@\n    (PossibleZeroQ[qValues[#]] & /@ \
qZeroTriples),\n  \"RawQSU2InvariantRelation\" -> TrueQ[FullSimplify[\n    \
qValues[{1, 2, 4}] - Cos[theta] qValues[{1, 2, 5}]] == 0]\n|>;\n\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- *)\n(* \
3. Static Delta1 and Delta2 direction and the factor alphaPrime/8      *)\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- \
*)\n\n$Assumptions = $Assumptions && H1 > 0 && H2 > 0 && H3 > 0;\npvec = \
Array[pv, 4];\nmvec = Array[mv, 4];\nzvec = Array[zv, 4];\ndot4[u_, v_] := \
Sum[u[[i]] v[[i]], {i, 4}];\np2 = dot4[pvec, pvec];\nm2 = dot4[mvec, \
mvec];\nz2 = dot4[zvec, zvec];\npm = dot4[pvec, mvec];\n\nnStatic = \
5;\ntIndex = 1;\nspatial = Range[2, 5];\ngStatic0 = DiagonalMatrix[\n  \
Join[{-1/(H1 H2)}, ConstantArray[H3, 4]]];\ngStaticInverse0 = \
Simplify[Inverse[gStatic0]];\nSetAttributes[setAnti2Static, \
HoldFirst];\nsetAnti2Static[x_, i_, j_, value_] :=\n  (x[[i, j]] = value; \
x[[j, i]] = -value;);\nfPlusStatic = ConstantArray[0, {nStatic, \
nStatic}];\nfMinusStatic = ConstantArray[0, {nStatic, nStatic}];\nDo[\n  \
setAnti2Static[fPlusStatic, tIndex, spatial[[i]],\n    (pvec[[i]] - \
mvec[[i]])/Sqrt[H1 H2]];\n  setAnti2Static[fMinusStatic, tIndex, \
spatial[[i]],\n    (pvec[[i]] + mvec[[i]])/Sqrt[H1 H2]],\n  {i, \
4}];\n\ndSigmaStatic = Join[{0}, (pvec - mvec)/2];\ndSigmaUpStatic = \
Simplify[gStaticInverse0.dSigmaStatic];\nhStatic0 = ConstantArray[0, \
{nStatic, nStatic, nStatic}];\nDo[hStatic0[[spatial[[i]], spatial[[j]], \
spatial[[k]]]] =\n   Sum[Signature[{i, j, k, l}] H3 zvec[[l]], {l, 4}],\n  \
{i, 4}, {j, 4}, {k, 4}];\n\nfSecondRaisedStatic[f_, mu_, nu_] := Sum[\n  \
f[[mu, lam]] gStaticInverse0[[lam, rho]] f[[nu, rho]],\n  {lam, nStatic}, \
{rho, nStatic}];\nfSquareStatic[f_] := Sum[\n  f[[mu, nu]] \
gStaticInverse0[[mu, rho]]\n    gStaticInverse0[[nu, sig]] f[[rho, sig]],\n  \
{mu, nStatic}, {nu, nStatic}, {rho, nStatic}, {sig, \
nStatic}];\nhOneDownTwoUpStatic[mu_, nu_, rho_] := Sum[\n  \
gStaticInverse0[[nu, aa]] gStaticInverse0[[rho, bb]]\n    hStatic0[[mu, aa, \
bb]], {aa, nStatic}, {bb, nStatic}];\nhTwoDownStatic[mu_, nu_] := Sum[\n  \
hStatic0[[mu, rho, sig]] hOneDownTwoUpStatic[nu, rho, sig],\n  {rho, \
nStatic}, {sig, nStatic}];\nhSquareStatic = Sum[\n  hStatic0[[mu, nu, rho]] \
gStaticInverse0[[mu, aa]]\n    gStaticInverse0[[nu, bb]] \
gStaticInverse0[[rho, cc]]\n    hStatic0[[aa, bb, cc]],\n  {mu, nStatic}, \
{nu, nStatic}, {rho, nStatic},\n  {aa, nStatic}, {bb, nStatic}, {cc, \
nStatic}];\n\ndelta1Metric = Table[Simplify[\n  \
fSecondRaisedStatic[fMinusStatic, mu, nu] +\n  \
fSecondRaisedStatic[fPlusStatic, mu, nu] +\n  4 dSigmaStatic[[mu]] \
dSigmaStatic[[nu]]],\n  {mu, nStatic}, {nu, nStatic}];\ndelta1Varphi = \
Simplify[\n  (fSquareStatic[fMinusStatic] + fSquareStatic[fPlusStatic])/4 +\n \
 dSigmaStatic.gStaticInverse0.dSigmaStatic];\ncommonStatic = \
Table[Simplify[\n  4 Sum[fPlusStatic[[mu, nu]] dSigmaUpStatic[[nu]],\n      \
{nu, nStatic}] +\n  Sum[hOneDownTwoUpStatic[mu, nu, rho] fMinusStatic[[nu, \
rho]],\n      {nu, nStatic}, {rho, nStatic}]], {mu, nStatic}];\ndelta1A = \
Simplify[commonStatic/(2 Sqrt[H1/H2])];\ndelta1B = Simplify[-Sqrt[H1/H2] \
commonStatic/2];\nbStatic0 = Join[{-1/H2}, ConstantArray[0, \
4]];\ndelta1LowerTwoForm = Table[Simplify[\n  (bStatic0[[nu]] delta1A[[mu]] \
-\n    bStatic0[[mu]] delta1A[[nu]])/2],\n  {mu, nStatic}, {nu, \
nStatic}];\n\ntRaw = -pm/(4 H3);\ngRaw1 = ConstantArray[0, {nStatic, \
nStatic}];\ngRaw1[[tIndex, tIndex]] = Simplify[2 tRaw/(H1 \
H2)];\nDo[gRaw1[[spatial[[i]], spatial[[j]]]] =\n  KroneckerDelta[i, j] z2/4, \
{i, 4}, {j, 4}];\nvarphiRaw1 = Simplify[-tRaw/2 + z2/(8 H3)];\naRaw1 = \
Join[{Simplify[-2 tRaw/H1]}, ConstantArray[0, 4]];\nbRaw1 = Join[{Simplify[2 \
tRaw/H2]}, ConstantArray[0, 4]];\n\ngAfterDelta1 = Simplify[gRaw1 + \
delta1Metric/8];\nvarphiAfterDelta1 = Simplify[varphiRaw1 + \
delta1Varphi/8];\naAfterDelta1 = Simplify[aRaw1 + delta1A/8];\nbAfterDelta1 = \
Simplify[bRaw1 + delta1B/8];\n\ngTargetDelta1 = ConstantArray[0, {nStatic, \
nStatic}];\ngTargetDelta1[[tIndex, tIndex]] =\n  (p2 + m2 - 2 pm)/(4 H1 H2 \
H3);\nDo[gTargetDelta1[[spatial[[i]], spatial[[j]]]] =\n  KroneckerDelta[i, \
j] z2/4 -\n  (pvec[[i]] + mvec[[i]]) (pvec[[j]] + mvec[[j]])/8,\n  {i, 4}, \
{j, 4}];\nvarphiTargetDelta1 = (-3 p2 - 3 m2 + 2 pm + 4 z2)/(32 \
H3);\naTargetDelta1 = Join[\n  {(p2 + m2 + 2 pm)/(8 H1 H3)}, ConstantArray[0, \
4]];\nbTargetDelta1 = Join[\n  {-(p2 + m2 + 2 pm)/(8 H2 H3)}, \
ConstantArray[0, 4]];\n\ngAfterDelta2 = Simplify[gAfterDelta1 +\n  \
Table[hTwoDownStatic[mu, nu],\n    {mu, nStatic}, {nu, \
nStatic}]/8];\nvarphiAfterDelta2 = Simplify[varphiAfterDelta1 + \
hSquareStatic/32];\ngTargetDelta2 = ConstantArray[0, {nStatic, \
nStatic}];\ngTargetDelta2[[tIndex, tIndex]] = gTargetDelta1[[tIndex, \
tIndex]];\nDo[gTargetDelta2[[spatial[[i]], spatial[[j]]]] =\n  \
KroneckerDelta[i, j] z2/2 -\n  (pvec[[i]] + mvec[[i]]) (pvec[[j]] + \
mvec[[j]])/8 -\n  zvec[[i]] zvec[[j]]/4, {i, 4}, {j, 4}];\nvarphiTargetDelta2 \
=\n  (-3 p2 - 3 m2 + 2 pm + 10 z2)/(32 H3);\n\nfieldRedefinitionLedger = <|\n \
 \"Delta1MetricUsesPlusAlphaPrimeOverEight\" ->\n    zeroTensorQ[gAfterDelta1 \
- gTargetDelta1],\n  \"Delta1VarphiUsesPlusAlphaPrimeOverEight\" ->\n    \
TrueQ[Simplify[varphiAfterDelta1 - varphiTargetDelta1] == 0],\n  \
\"Delta1MomentumVectorUsesPlusAlphaPrimeOverEight\" ->\n    \
zeroTensorQ[aAfterDelta1 - aTargetDelta1],\n  \
\"Delta1WindingVectorUsesPlusAlphaPrimeOverEight\" ->\n    \
zeroTensorQ[bAfterDelta1 - bTargetDelta1],\n  \
\"Delta1LowerTwoFormStaticShiftVanishes\" ->\n    \
zeroTensorQ[delta1LowerTwoForm],\n  \
\"Delta2MetricUsesPlusAlphaPrimeOverEight\" ->\n    zeroTensorQ[gAfterDelta2 \
- gTargetDelta2],\n  \"Delta2VarphiUsesPlusAlphaPrimeOverEight\" ->\n    \
TrueQ[Simplify[varphiAfterDelta2 - varphiTargetDelta2] == 0],\n  \
\"Delta2LeavesStaticVectorsUnchanged\" ->\n    zeroTensorQ[aAfterDelta1 - \
aTargetDelta1] &&\n    zeroTensorQ[bAfterDelta1 - bTargetDelta1],\n  \
\"StaticThreeFormUnchangedByDelta1\" -> \
zeroTensorQ[delta1LowerTwoForm]\n|>;\n\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- *)\n(* \
4. Signature, curvature, and unchanged-alphaPrime bridge               *)\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- \
*)\n\n(* A lower three-form and the metric both reverse sign between the \
source\n   mostly-minus convention and the STU mostly-plus convention.  \
Raising one\n   index therefore leaves the mixed torsion matrix unchanged. \
*)\nomegaHet = Array[omegaHetComponent, {2, 2}];\nhMixedHet = \
Array[hMixedHetComponent, {2, 2}];\nomegaSTU = -omegaHet;\nhMixedSTU = \
hMixedHet;\nomegaMinusHet = omegaHet - hMixedHet/2;\nomegaPlusSTU = omegaSTU \
+ hMixedSTU/2;\nconnectionBridgePass = zeroTensorQ[omegaPlusSTU + \
omegaMinusHet];\n\n(* The two Cartan curvature conventions are opposite.  \
Substituting the\n   connection bridge gives \
R_STU(OmegaPlus)=-R_het(omegaMinus). *)\ndOmegaMinusHet = \
Array[dOmegaMinusHetComponent, {2, 2}];\nrHet = dOmegaMinusHet - \
omegaMinusHet.omegaMinusHet;\nrSTU = -dOmegaMinusHet + \
omegaMinusHet.omegaMinusHet;\ncurvatureBridgePass = zeroTensorQ[rSTU + \
rHet];\ncurvatureSquarePass = TrueQ[Expand[\n  Tr[rSTU.rSTU] - Tr[rHet.rHet]] \
== 0];\n\n(* The static profiles provide a physical, component-level check \
that the\n   metric-sign bridge does not reverse alphaPrime. \
*)\nzPlusStaticCorrection = -2 qplus qminus/\n  (r^2 (r^2 + qzero) (r^2 + \
qminus));\ndLog[f_] := D[Log[f], r];\ntBH = -dLog[hp] dLog[hm]/(4 h0);\nsZero \
= dLog[h0]^2;\ngtt2606Relative = \
Simplify[-zPlusStaticCorrection/hp];\ngttBHRelative = Simplify[-2 \
tBH];\ngSpatial2606Relative = \
Simplify[zZeroCorrection/h0];\ngSpatialBHRelative = Simplify[sZero/(4 \
h0)];\nphi2606 = Simplify[\n  zZeroCorrection/(2 h0) - \
zPlusStaticCorrection/(4 hp)];\nphiBH = Simplify[-tBH/2 + sZero/(8 \
h0)];\naTime2606 = Simplify[-zPlusStaticCorrection/hp^2];\naTimeBH = \
Simplify[-2 tBH/hp];\n\nsignatureAlphaLedger = <|\n  \
\"SignatureTorsionConnectionBridge\" -> connectionBridgePass,\n  \
\"SignatureCurvatureBridge\" -> curvatureBridgePass,\n  \
\"CurvatureQuadraticInvariantUnchanged\" -> curvatureSquarePass,\n  \
\"StaticGttKeepsAlphaPrimeSign\" ->\n    TrueQ[FullSimplify[gtt2606Relative - \
gttBHRelative] == 0],\n  \"StaticSpatialMetricKeepsAlphaPrimeSign\" ->\n    \
TrueQ[FullSimplify[gSpatial2606Relative - gSpatialBHRelative] == 0],\n  \
\"StaticDilatonKeepsAlphaPrimeSign\" ->\n    TrueQ[FullSimplify[phi2606 - \
phiBH] == 0],\n  \"StaticMomentumPotentialKeepsAlphaPrimeSign\" ->\n    \
TrueQ[FullSimplify[aTime2606 - aTimeBH] == 0],\n  \"StaticZplusIdentity\" \
->\n    TrueQ[FullSimplify[zPlusStaticCorrection/hp - 2 tBH] == 0],\n  \
\"StaticZzeroIdentity\" -> TrueQ[FullSimplify[\n    zZeroCorrection/h0 - \
sZero/(4 h0)] == 0]\n|>;\n\nledger = Join[horizontalLeadingLedger, \
horizontalFirstOrderLedger,\n  qLedger, fieldRedefinitionLedger, \
signatureAlphaLedger];\nfinalPass = And @@ \
Values[ledger];\n\nPrint[\"CONSOLIDATED_LEDGER = \", \
InputForm[ledger]];\nPrint[\"LEADING_HORIZONTAL_FIELD = -M_het + (Hplus \
Hminus)^(-1) dOmega wedge Theta\"];\nPrint[\"FIRST_ORDER_HORIZONTAL_FIELD = \
-M1-K1 wedge A0-G0 wedge A1\"];\nPrint[\"CORRECTED_Q_NONZERO = \", \
InputForm[qNonzero]];\nPrint[\"FIELD_REDEFINITION_DIRECTION = Phi_after = \
Phi_before + alphaPrime DeltaPhi/8\"];\nPrint[\"TORSION_CONNECTION_BRIDGE = \
OmegaPlus_STU = -omegaMinus_heterotic\"];\nPrint[\"ALPHAPRIME_SIGN_UNCHANGED \
= \", And @@ Values[signatureAlphaLedger]];\nPrint[\"FINAL_PASS = \", \
finalPass];"], "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1400, 900}, 
 StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"]
